00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.980
If you were just dropped in this place with
no prior knowledge, where would you guess

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:21.520
you were? Maybe Florida or California o r
Hawaii—somewhere tropical but this is definitely

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:27.000
the US. It just looks like the US. From the
style of signs to the way the roads look to

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.590
the stores that line the streets, you can
tell it’s the US but it’s not Florida,

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.630
it’s not California, it’s not Hawaii,
it’s not even on this side of the world.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.790
It’s America’s most isolated territory.
It’s Guam.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:47.690
The United States has five inhabited territories—the
US Virgin Islands, Puerto Rico, American Samoa,

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:52.200
the Northern Mariana Islands, and Guam itself.
Guam is the furthest of these five from the

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:58.850
continental US—nearly 8,000 miles away from
Washington, DC—making it the most isolated.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:05.059
Beijing, Delhi, Cape Town, and Buenos Aires
are all closer to DC than Guam is and yet

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:11.670
the island is a fully fledged territory of
the US. It is the US. Guam has been inhabited

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.409
for thousands of years by the native Chamorro
people until the 1500s when it was first claimed

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.950
as a territory by Spain. Centuries later,
after the US’ victory in the Spanish-American

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:25.529
war, the territory was ceded to the United
States along with Puerto Rico and the Philippines.

00:01:25.529 --> 00:01:30.099
Aside from a brief and brutal Japanese occupation
during World War Two, the island has remained

00:01:30.099 --> 00:01:35.420
part of the US ever since. Many Americans
had never even heard of Guam until summer

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.590
2017. That was when North Korean leader Kim
Jong-un threatened to launch a ballistic missile

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:46.100
at Guam. The threats may have since subsided,
but the effects of that summer have not.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:49.829
The island stretches less than 30 miles from
top to bottom which makes it smaller than

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:55.649
every other US state and territory and yet
it packs more than 160,000 people into that

00:01:55.649 --> 00:02:02.220
small size. In fact, it’s more densely populated
than all but five US states or territories.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:08.099
Meanwhile, it is by far the most developed
place in Micronesia. To put it in perspective,

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:11.600
Guam’s neighboring islands, the Northern
Mariana Islands, which are also part of the

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:19.080
US, have a GDP per capita of $16,800 while
Guam’s is more than $35,000. Kiribati, meanwhile,

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:27.700
the most populous county in Micronesia, has
a GDP per capita of $1,500. Guam is an outpost

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.780
of the modern, developed world in one of the
poorest regions of the world. Its location

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:38.270
though, is its greatest asset. It’s economy
exists because of where it is.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:42.810
The island is three hours from Tokyo, four
hours from Seoul, and five hours from Hong

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:48.990
Kong. It’s close to Asia but it is still
the US—unequivocally. You see American license

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:52.700
plates, American school buses, American-style
ambulances, they have US post offices, they

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:58.160
use the US dollar, they have American stores,
American hotels, US National Parks, US airlines.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:04.750
There is no compromise on the American-ness
of Guam because it is the US. They fly the

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:09.850
US flag and for tourists, this is a draw.
Instead of flying seven hours to Hawaii or

00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:14.960
ten hours to California, Japanese tourists
can and do just fly three hours to Guam in

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:20.240
order to visit the US. The malls, which look
identical to any in Virginia or Kansas or

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.930
anywhere else in the US, are hugely popular
with Asian tourists as they can buy American

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:30.180
goods for a fraction of what they would cost
in Asia. About 1.5 million people visit the

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:36.620
island of 160 thousand each year, but what’s
not good for tourism is missile threats. “Last

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:45.280
summer when they were playing ‘who’s missile’s
bigger’ we were the ones who suffered, you

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:53.120
know, our tourism took a huge nosedive that
month of August. We never saw so many news

00:03:53.120 --> 00:04:00.140
agencies coming to Guam from countries that
didn’t even realize we existed because all

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:05.810
of a sudden Kim Jung Un was threatening the
American territory in the Pacific.” (17:39)

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:10.620
This is Benjamin Cruz, speaker of the Guam
Legislature. As he said, the island’s economy

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:15.181
suffered immensely from the North Korean missile
threat. Many visitors of Guam come as parts

00:04:15.181 --> 00:04:19.609
of school groups or corporate retreats and
these groups in particular almost universally

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:29.320
cancelled their trips. “We lost, I mean,
almost all of Japan stopped coming. I mean,

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:33.919
everybody was afraid to come, the only ones
that were coming were the news media.” (28:00)

00:04:33.919 --> 00:04:38.389
Fortunately, the effects were partially mitigated
by an increase in visitors from South Korea

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:42.300
who were less worried about missile threats
since its a reality they live every day back

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.520
home, but for an island so centered around
tourism, being dragged into politics is never

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.610
good.
Despite being part of the US, though, Guam

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:55.650
functions politically differently from every
other part of the US. Benjamin Cruz, along

00:04:55.650 --> 00:05:00.460
with the 14 other senators, are the lawmakers
of Guam. They can legislate just like any

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.930
state legislature, but the main political
difference for Guam is at the federal level.

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:09.409
All the US federal laws, the ones made in
Washington for the whole country, all those

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:15.529
laws apply in Guam. What Guam doesn’t get
though, is a vote. Their congressional representatives

00:05:15.529 --> 00:05:20.449
don’t get a vote so by extension, the people
of Guam can't vote on the laws that apply

00:05:20.449 --> 00:05:25.780
to them. In addition, unlike Washington, DC,
which also does’t receive a vote in Congress,

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:30.400
Guam, along with the other US territories,
is not able to vote for their president—the

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:35.460
US president. This presents an issue not only
because of the lapse in democracy, but also

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:40.370
because many US laws that may make sense for
the continental United States just don’t

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:46.689
for a territory on the other side of the world.
“We’d like to be able to invite people

00:05:46.689 --> 00:05:54.529
to the island and industries and not have
to worry about whether the SEC would approve

00:05:54.529 --> 00:06:01.039
it or the FCC would approve it. We’d like
to be able to have control over our skies

00:06:01.039 --> 00:06:08.009
so we can invite airlines to fly in without
having to clear with FAA on whether or not

00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:12.939
this airline or that airline can or cannot
fly.” (13:10) The process for a foreign

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:17.099
airline of gaining approval to fly to the
US is often long and laborious and there are

00:06:17.099 --> 00:06:21.349
a number of special security and immigration
rules for flights to the US. This isn’t

00:06:21.349 --> 00:06:26.010
a problem for large, intercontinental airlines
or Mexican or Canadian ones for whom flights

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.249
to the US represent a large part of their
market, but for small regional Asian carriers,

00:06:30.249 --> 00:06:35.339
they might pass on flights to Guam just to
avoid having to gain FAA approval.

00:06:35.339 --> 00:06:40.100
Another issue for Guam is the Jones Act. This
law prevents foreign built, owned, or operated

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:45.639
ships from carrying cargo or passengers between
US ports. This may make sense within the continental

00:06:45.639 --> 00:06:49.789
United States. Just as you wouldn’t want
a foreign airline flying domestic cargo routes

00:06:49.789 --> 00:06:53.949
you wouldn’t want a foreign shipping company
taking over cargo routes like Houston to Charleston

00:06:53.949 --> 00:06:59.270
or Seattle to Oakland but Guam is a different
story. Cargo ships generally make many stops

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:03.499
along their routes so it would be perfectly
normal for a Taiwanese ship, for example,

00:07:03.499 --> 00:07:08.880
to go from Oakland to Hawaii to Guam to Osaka
to Taipei but it can’t because then it’d

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:15.080
be transporting goods between US ports. Instead,
only US ships can bring goods from the US,

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:20.160
where most of Guam’s goods come from, to
Guam. Other US territories like American Samoa

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:24.460
and the Northern Mariana Islands are exempt
from this rule but Guam is still subject to

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:27.600
it which makes shipping to the island more
expensive.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:32.120
Despite the issues the US federal government
may cause, the people of Guam are in no hurry

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:38.469
to distance themselves from it. “I think
if you were to ask a majority of the people

00:07:38.469 --> 00:07:45.740
on the island they would like to have a closer
union with the United States and some may

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:52.300
even want statehood. In fact, a majority of
them would like to see statehood.” (5:00)

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:58.240
In many ways, Guam is one of the most patriotic
areas in the US. The US military freed Guam

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:03.069
from a brutal and deadly Japanese occupation
during World War Two which many of the older

00:08:03.069 --> 00:08:09.089
residents still remember. The younger residents,
meanwhile, quite often work for the US. “Just

00:08:09.089 --> 00:08:14.939
about every family on this island, I’m sure
almost every family on this island had at

00:08:14.939 --> 00:08:18.740
least one member of their family serve in
the military.” (11:40) One out of eight

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:24.349
residents of Guam serve or have served in
the US armed forces. It has a higher enlistment

00:08:24.349 --> 00:08:29.809
rate than any US state but this is helped
by the fact that a quarter of the island is

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:35.191
US military bases. The island is one of the
US military’s most strategic assets. Of

00:08:35.191 --> 00:08:40.490
course the US has plenty of bases in Japan
and South Korea but Guam is US soil less than

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:45.290
four hours away from North Korea, the East
China Sea, and the South China Sea—all possible

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:50.530
flash-points for US conflict. The US military
is the single largest employer on Guam and

00:08:50.530 --> 00:08:55.361
its economy depends on the military. While
tourism may have suffered recently, the military

00:08:55.361 --> 00:09:00.270
business is good. The number of military personnel
stationed on Guam is slated to more than double

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:05.030
in the coming decade which will no doubt stimulate
the economy. This doesn’t come without concern,

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:10.140
Guam only has so much land, but all factors
considered, Guam is on the rise.

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:15.390
Guam is truly a unique place. Plenty of countries
have territories far away from their mainland

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:20.090
but few are as developed and as similar to
the rest of the country as Guam. If Guam was

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:24.750
just off the coast of the US mainland it would
be totally unremarkable—just another piece

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:29.180
of the US that looks and acts like the rest
of the US—but it’s not. It’s on the

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:34.560
other side of the world. Guam is a relic of
colonialism but today it’s a thriving, developed

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.720
place. It may not get treated like the US
even by its own government, but in all other

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:44.800
ways, Guam is the United States.
One aspect of Guam’s story that this video

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:48.160
